#sleela 1.12
// A newer MINOR within the same MAJOR. Per SL-META-0001 Section 4.4, MINOR
// increments only ADD constructs, so a lower-syntax program is forward-declarable
// as a higher minor only if the compiler supports it. This file sits one minor
// above the current ceiling (max supported = 1.11, which added nested classes),
// so it is still "too new" and MUST be rejected -- proving MINOR is enforced too.
class MinorAhead {
    void main() {
        print("unreachable on a 1.0 compiler");
    }
}
